      "moduleId": "rn_zC7QWr77fGFWbhNS::L1",
      "stem": "Explain why height in humans forms a continuous spread rather than two classes.",
      "misconceptionClass": "mechanism reasoning",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "Several height genes each add their own contribution, so the many possible allele combinations blend into a continuous range from short to tall.",
