    {
      "id": "rn_zC7QWr77fGFWbhNS::L1::Q9",
      "moduleId": "rn_zC7QWr77fGFWbhNS::L1",
      "stem": "A student measures the heights of fifty classmates and finds a smooth spread with no two clear groups. What does the pattern suggest about the inheritance of height, and why is a Punnett square the wrong tool here?",
      "misconceptionClass": "scenario application",
      "kind": "application",
      "modelAnswer": "The smooth spread suggests polygenic inheritance, and the square is the wrong tool because its four cells cannot represent the many allele combinations several genes produce.",
